Dear Robert,

Please find the Q1 2020 inspection status for the ATU-100. The current activities are being managed according to the intervals defined in QSCP-IP-ATU100 Rev 3, which specifies 3 years for Class 1 sour gas, regenerator overhead and rich amine, and 6 years for the remaining lines.

The thickness data for the 150 CMLs is based on the re-baseline survey completed by Larkhall NDE Services Inc., as detailed in LNDE-RPT-20191001-027-R0. We are utilizing these values to monitor the remaining life and schedule subsequent readings per site rules.

